Article 9 The procuratorial personnel appearing before the court shall perform the following duties:
(1) reading the indictment of public interest litigation;
(2) presenting and explaining the evidence collected and investigated by the People's Procuratorate, and cross-examining relevant evidence;
(3) participating in the court investigation, conducting debate, and expressing opinions;
(4) engaging in other litigation activities according to law.

Article 14 Where the People's Procuratorate initiates a civil public interest action, it shall submit the following materials:
(1) an indictment of civil public interest action, together with copies according to the number of defendants;
(2) preliminary evidence materials proving that the defendant's act has already harmed the social public interests;
(3) evidence materials proving that the procuratorial organ has completed the pre-litigation announcement procedure.

Article 22 Where the People's Procuratorate initiates an administrative public interest action, it shall submit the following materials:
(1) an indictment of administrative public interest action, together with copies according to the number of defendants;
(2) evidence materials proving that the defendant's illegal exercise of powers or failure to perform duties has caused harm to national interests or social public interests;
(3) evidence materials proving that the procuratorial organ has completed the pre-litigation procedure and the administrative organ has failed to perform its duties according to law or to correct its illegal acts.

Article 25 The People's Court shall render a judgment in an administrative public interest action distinguishing among the following circumstances:
(1) where the administrative act being sued falls under any of the circumstances set forth in Articles 74 or 75 of the Administrative Procedure Law, it shall render a judgment confirming the illegality or invalidity, and may simultaneously render a judgment ordering the administrative organ to take remedial measures;
(2) where the administrative act being sued falls under any of the circumstances set forth in Article 70 of the Administrative Procedure Law, it shall render a judgment revoking or partially revoking the act, and may render a judgment ordering the defendant administrative organ to make a new administrative act;
(3) where the defendant administrative organ fails to perform its statutory duties, it shall render a judgment ordering the performance within a specified period;
(4) where the administrative penalty imposed by the defendant administrative organ is clearly inappropriate, or there is a definite error in determining or confirming the amount involved in other administrative acts, it shall render a judgment modifying the act;
(5) where the administrative act being sued has conclusive evidence, correctly applies laws and regulations, complies with statutory procedures, does not exceed authority, does not abuse power, and is not clearly inappropriate, or the grounds on which the People's Procuratorate requests the defendant administrative organ to perform its statutory duties are not established, it shall render a judgment dismissing the litigation claims.
The People's Court may notify the government to which the defendant administrative organ belongs or other relevant functional departments of the judgment result.
